            "review_text": "LeyQuyDonStudents\n4 contributions\n0\nEnjoy Seafood on a Floating Boat\nSep 2015\nLocation: Hoa Hoa (which means \"Double Flowers\" in Vietnamese) is on a floating boat at the entrance to a harbor.\n\nService: The restaurant is always crowded but has fast service. It has an English menu for foreign guests. Most of the staff members are male and they are really handsome. In addition to the appearance, they are professional and friendly. \n\nFood: The seafood is carefully selected so it is extremely fresh, and delicious. There are some dishes you cannot miss, such as jellyfish soup and seafood hot pot. Moreover, the restaurant gives a bonus of dessert.\nRead more\nWritten March 24, 2016",
