            "review_title": "Review at Hoa Hoa Restaurant",
            "review_text": "lthyen75\nHanoi, Vietnam157 contributions\n0\nA very local way of total fresh seafood served on a boat-restaurant\nJul 2015 • Friends\nRestaurants in Quy Nhon were not high class like in other hot-spot places in Vietnam, but in return, the dishes were excellent and the prices were reasonable. Hoa Hoa Floating restaurant was exactly a good example of it. All the seafood are served from fresh to table, at an extraodinary fast-speed service, they all very tasty.\n\nWe ordered fresh jelly fish salad with green mango, snail (Ốc nhảy) clam (Xìa, local name), steam eeggy squid, cheese-baked oyster, fried grouper with tamarind sauce (head for the rice soup) and they all nicely cooked. \n\nThis seems to be an expensive restaurant in town already but all we can have is lovely food and good services, still cheaper than many good restaurants in other cities. Should definitely try it at least once :)\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 29, 2015",
